{
  "case_id": "2017-17-586",
  "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Appellants (Scott A. Keller)",
      "case_id": "2017-17-586",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b6d559c38fa-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Texas legislature did not have a racially discriminatory purpose when it adopted the entire court-ordered congressional remedial plan and virtually all of the remedial state house plan."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-586",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b6d559c38fa-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So could you address the -- our jurisdiction first?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-586",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b6d559c38fa-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So tell me why that's not true -- why that's not the case under Gunn."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-17-586",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b6d559c38fa-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: It seems as though that that's a -- you're essentially saying that this PI opinion was a safe harbor for the state. And that seems an odd thing to say."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2017-17-586",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b6d559c38fa-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I do want to address the merits, but if I could make a -- a few points about jurisdiction at the outset to show why this case is different from other cases that may arise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-586",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b6d559c38fa-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the court gave only three days to the state legislature, which is not -- which is far from sufficient time to allow a sovereign state to engage in the critical act of deciding whether to reapportion the legislature."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "District Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-586",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b6d559c38fa-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district court said: \"The plaintiffs can establish their claim by showing that the legislature adopted the 2013 plans with a discriminatory purpose, maintained the district lines with a discriminatory purpose, or intentionally furthered preexisting intentional discrimination.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Appelltees",
      "case_id": "2017-17-586",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b6d559c38fa-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HICKS: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I hadn't anticipated doing this, but I'm going to start with the jurisdictional question, which, of course, is what you all start with."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-17-586",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b6d559c38fa-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Could -- could Texas have -- have used the current maps for the 2018 elections?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-17-586",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b6d559c38fa-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think we lack jurisdiction if the order doesn't contain the word \"injunction\" or \"order\" but has the practical effect of doing that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-17-586",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b6d559c38fa-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Has -- has the practical effects been applied in the 1253 context as distinguished from 1292?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Allison J. Riggs",
      "case_id": "2017-17-586",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b6d559c38fa-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court does not have jurisdiction to hear this appeal, but if it proceeds to the merits, the district court properly applied the Arlington Heights framework to analyze the intent of the 2013 legislature in reenacting some of the same state house districts it had deliberately designed in 2011 to cancel out or minimize the voting strength of black and Latino voters in Texas."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-17-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b6d559c38fa-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: -- what room is left between our VRA jurisprudence under Section 2 and the Fourteenth Amendment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Appellants (Mr. Keller)",
      "case_id": "2017-17-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b6d559c38fa3dd0d8b665794cef64017daee86a800f48b351f00c4ea6e23dd9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b6d559c38fa-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KELLER: That's right, and I'll turn to racial gerrymandering in HD90, that would be the one district we did change. And, by the way, if we had changed other districts, then we would have been subjected to all sorts of additional legal challenges, which is exactly why the legislature acted in good faith in adopting the congressional map wholesale and virtually all the State House map."
    },
